ain (warn-only; the Cut tab shows it as a ⚡ chip on the Strategy row, and a click switches the strategy, step G-D). Sentry: `a_retired_clearing_strategy_is_named_r2`. Option **Contour each level** (`contour_each_level`, C4, operator ruling D69 2026-10-28; off by default, and off the output is unchanged): on a rest rough (remaining stock) with a machining boundary, after each level one contour runs along the boundary where stock the tool can reach still stands beyond it, never more than one Depth/Pass under any stock in reach, so the next level does not cut it deeper (G-RESTDOC); short gaps on one ring join by the machine's feed-or-retract rule, and a contour cut over the pass load carries a feed cap. Corne play job: the edge op's volume over Depth/Pass 6750 → 3138 mm³, job time +19 %. In Global order a fresh rough is unchanged. In By Area order (C4b, the F9 fix) the option also cuts the walls of each region at each of its levels, keeping every cut off another region's material above the level; with the option off By Area cuts the walls once, at the bottom, as before. Sentries: `a_rest_op_holds_one_depth_at_the_band_c4`, `contour_each_level_is_off_by_default_c4`, `by_area_walls_cut_each_region_level_c4b`. Rest region filter (`rest_max_region_area_mm2`, `rest_max_region_width_mm`, 2026-11-02; both empty by default, and empty the output is unchanged): on a rest rough (remaining stock), at each level a region of remaining material is cut only when its area is at most the area bound and its width (the diameter of the largest circle inside it, read on the planner grid to one cell) is at most the width bound. A region that fails is skipped at that level, not clipped, so a small tool cuts only the narrow valleys and corners that a larger tool could not reach. Both strategies and the Contour Parallel cleanup read the same filtered grid. A value of 0 or less refuses at the parameter door. The GUI shows the two rows (Max region width, Max region area) on a rest rough or while set. Sentry: `--lib rest_filter`. Strategy **Geodesic Adaptive** (`clearing_strategy = "geodesic_adaptive"`, integration step 7.4, 2026-10-28): NEW, NOT YET MACHINE-TESTED. Each slice piece is planned by the geodesic-wavefront plan (`adaptive::geodesic`, preset C35 plan A); the passes hold the pass load, the step split reads the stock depth, a keep-down link is routed at the cut feed, and each tight turn and plunge departure carries a feed cap (`Move::feed_cap`) from the larger of its swept width and its removal per mm; since P22f-2a (2026-11-10) every other fed step is also read on the planner's 3D stock and is capped where it meets more than the pass load (up to a slot) or split where it meets more. A capped move draws dashed in every move colour mode of the 3D view (legend entry "dashed: fed at a load cap"); the move count's hover on the Generate row gives the planned count and the lowest cap; MCP `get_cut_trace` carries `capped_move_count`, `capped_min_feed_mm_min` and the bounded `capped_moves` rows (step G-B, 2026-10-28). It clears the body only; a piece it cannot plan is left for a rest op (follow it with a Contour Parallel rest op; a "Rest regions of …" boundary on that op takes the regions it left, see rest analysis below). The usual roughing parameters only. Each region opens on its own grown outline, so the passes reach the region edge under the pass load; with a tool over 6.6 mm the arm cut a full-slot loop round each region before P22f-1 (2026-11-10), and now does so only where the outline cannot be grown (a split, the measured margin or the closing guard; the generation record `Produced::region_openings` names each case; sentry `a_geodesic_slice_cuts_no_full_slot_sweep_p22f`). An older build refuses a project file that names it. Sentries: `geodesic_adaptive_keeps_the_research_geometry_s7_4`, `a_geodesic_cap_survives_every_dressup_s7_4`, `adaptive3d_emission_byte_parity` (case `geodesic_adaptive`) Left stock (P37, 2026-11-16): the planner records each region or piece that it holds as material and does not plan (under the small-area bound, under Min Region Cut Length, no Geodesic Adaptive field). When one still holds stock at the end of the plan, the op raises `geom.rough_left_stock` (Caution, a warning): the counts, the area, the tallest stock and its position, and whether the op publishes its rest regions for a toolpath boundary. The export names it in the G-code header and in `summary.json` (`Gate::RoughLeftStock`). It does not count a strip narrower than the tool radius at a wall. Sentry: `--lib _p37` |
